PRODUCTION DEFECT IN THIS ROW'S FILE, found by task-80322112 (child 3, the browser proof) driving the REAL command from a real browser. `repository.bootstrap` CANNOT SUCCEED ON A REAL FILESYSTEM. Filing here per task rail 3 (a command defect is child 2's); the fix row is task-4a9dd0ff (see below). No edit made to your file.

WHAT THE BROWSER SAW. Playwright, real daemon, empty store, local-only path (GitHub fields empty). The identity fence now admits the paired HUMAN (task-6d5db404 landed 2735406c), so the run gets all the way to the effects and then answers:

  BOOTSTRAP_CATALOG_FAILED at DAEMON_INGRESS

THE CAUSE, at repository-bootstrap-command.ts:174-179. The `registerCatalog` port you wire builds:
  configPath: `${repository.dir}/moe.config.json`
  storePath:  `${repository.dir}/.moe-next/store.sqlite`
Neither path is ever created. `git grep -n "moe\.config\.json" apps/daemon/src --include=*.ts` (excluding tests) returns EXACTLY TWO hits: `cli/moe-init.ts:34` which merely NAMES the constant, and your line :176 which consumes it. Nothing on the bootstrap path writes it, and nothing creates `.moe-next/`. The controlled-profile scaffold does not emit them either - its full emitted set is package.json, pnpm-workspace.yaml, pnpm-lock.yaml, tsconfig.base.json, vite.config.ts, playwright.config.ts, docker-compose.yml, .gitignore, .env.example, README.md, .github/workflows/ci.yml, migrations/, e2e/, packages/api/*, packages/web/* - no moe.config.json, no .moe-next.

`project-catalog.ts:127-140 canonicalEntry` then realpaths configPath and dirname(storePath); both ENOENT, so it refuses PROJECT_CATALOG_PATH_UNRESOLVED, `project-catalog-registrar.ts:67` THROWS it, and `repository-bootstrap-service.ts:66-67` catches a throwing port and answers BOOTSTRAP_CATALOG_FAILED / CATALOG_FAILED_LOCAL_REPOSITORY_RETAINED. The local repository is retained and committed - only the catalog step fails - so the operator gets a hard ERROR for a repository that is actually fine.

WHY YOUR ARMS STAY GREEN. `repository-bootstrap-journey.test.ts:114,127` takes `Omit<RepositoryBootstrapSeams, "catalog">` and stubs `catalog:` with an in-memory recorder. The real `createNodeProjectCatalogRegistrar` is never exercised, so the realpath requirement is invisible to every unit arm, including :241 "SUCCEEDS local-only with gh absent: committed, bound, catalogued".

PROBE, full source so it can be recreated (global rail 12). Ran under node v24 type-stripping from %TEMP%, deleted in the same call:

  const mod = await import(pathToFileURL(
    "D:/projexts/moe-next/apps/daemon/src/projects/project-catalog-registrar.ts").href);
  const dir = mkdtempSync(join(tmpdir(), "probe-cat-"));
  const register = mod.createNodeProjectCatalogRegistrar(join(dir, "catalog.json"));
  const input = { configPath: `${dir}/moe.config.json`, projectId: "p1",
    root: dir, storePath: `${dir}/.moe-next/store.sqlite`, title: "probe-product" };
  try { await register(input); console.log("A: REGISTERED_OK"); }
  catch (e) { console.log("A: THREW", e.name, e.code); }
  writeFileSync(input.configPath, "{}"); mkdirSync(join(dir, ".moe-next"), { recursive: true });
  try { await register(input); console.log("CONTROL: REGISTERED_OK"); }
  catch (e) { console.log("CONTROL: THREW", e.name, e.code); }

OUTPUT, with the discriminating control:
  A_SCAFFOLD_SHAPED_INPUT: THREW ProjectCatalogRefusalError PROJECT_CATALOG_PATH_UNRESOLVED
  CONTROL_PATHS_EXIST: REGISTERED_OK
Per-path: root RESOLVES, configPath ENOENT, dirname(storePath) ENOENT.

SHAPE OF THE FIX (the fix row's call, not mine). It belongs in your composition at :174-179, not in the scaffold and not in the catalog: moe.config.json and .moe-next/ are MOE's own project files, not the generated product's, and `cli/moe-init.ts` already knows how to write the config. Loosening `canonicalEntry` would weaken the catalog for every caller. Whichever way it goes, the arm that proves it must NOT stub the `catalog` seam.
